During the past decade, intense research efforts were observed for MOFs on gas separation. Some specific topics of gas separations have been reviewed in the past, including $\mathrm{CO}_{2}$ capture,[56–59] hydrocarbon separation,[60,61] noble gas separation,[62] separation of hydrogen isotopes,[63,64] and toxic gas removal.[65,66] In this review, we focus on select topics to illustrate how different features of MOFs can be utilized to address these challenges.
